how's it going everybody it's warren  welcome back to the cosmic wonder this  is going to be  my non-spoiler review of the falcon and  the winter soldier  episode 1. so there won't be any  spoilers about the episode in this video  but there are some very  important things that i think you should  know before going into the falcon and  the winter soldier series  this is a very very different show than  one division so  whether you liked one of vision or you  didn't like one division  here's a little information on what this  show is really like  and if you love marvel and you want to  stay up to date on all things mcu be  sure to subscribe so you don't miss out  on any of the latest videos  so a big question i have been getting is  is the falcon in the winter soldier  similar to one division and the answer  is no not only are these characters very  very different from each other but the  show is actually very different as well  one division was kind of this new  experiment that marvel did that i really  did enjoy  however some fans did say that even  though they did enjoy  one division it didn't really feel like  a marvel project  and if you feel that way i definitely  understand that the sitcom style type of  tv show  mixed with some dark undertones was kind  of new for everybody  but with the falcon and the winter  soldier right away you know  this is a marvel project it feels like a  marvel project  from everything down to the music to the  sound effects to the comedy to the  interaction between the characters to  the action  and to the reference of other characters  and the fact that this is entirely woven  inside of the mcu and that is referenced  and of course since this  is essentially a captain america  spin-off within the first couple of  minutes we see things relating to  captain america and there are some  pretty big scenes  involving good old cap not actually him  on screen so don't think that he's going  to show up but things that he's done  so right away it just feels like yes  another  marvel studios project another thing  that you need to know is that this  doesn't exactly feel like a tv show it  feels like a movie  now i know some people weren't exactly  thrilled about disney plus and  instead of them doing movies they're now  doing shows but keep in mind we're still  getting the same amount of movies and  they're adding the show so it's just  more content for us  but the series does feel like a movie  and that's because it had an  insanely big budget i think it was  rumored to be over 150 million dollars  and the way that director kari skoglyn  talked about shooting this series is she  said that they shot it  like a movie they shot six episodes so  six  hours worth of footage and then they  just edited it and cut it down to what  they wanted to show throughout these six  episodes  and i quite enjoyed it i did think that  it was very cinematic both  sam scenes and bucky scenes were both  done exceptionally well  it doesn't feel like it's any different  than actually watching a movie from the  graphics to the acting to the story  it feels like we're getting a captain  america spin-off movie that's based on  falcon and the winter soldier we're just  getting parts  one through six now the next thing i'll  talk about is the action in the show  a lot of really good action as you've  probably seen from the trailers there's  a lot of things that happen falcon  flying through the air helicopters  hand-to-hand combat they use guns they  use explosives  it's extremely fast-paced when they do  all of this and granted i've only seen  the first episode so far but everything  that they do involving the action  sequences and fighting is actually  pretty creative  the way that falcon fights and flies is  different than anything we've seen from  him in the past  and as we've seen from the trailers and  photos and promotions he does have a new  suit which they do talk about  now considering that this is the first  episode of the series and it's supposed  to be setting everything up they  actually do throw a  good amount of action in this episode  the episode is about 48 minutes long  now of course as disney has showed us  with one division the end credits are  about five minutes long  possibly even longer so let's go ahead  and say that there's 42 minutes of  actual footage  half of that is probably action  sequences with sam and bucky  but the other half has done  exceptionally well the story makes  a lot of sense it's very grounded it's  very real it addresses the questions  that we have all been wondering since  the end of avengers end game when  captain america gave sam the shield  and there's a reason for everything a  good reason behind  everything that takes place with sam and  with bucky because in the beginning  as most people know they have two  different stories throughout their time  together in the mcu they've had this  love-hate relationship they know each  other but their friends their teammates  they fought together alongside of their  best friend  captain america and they very much go  over each of their personal stories  before they get together in the first  episode and it's really cool to see  because this takes place a handful of  months after the events of avengers in  game  and of course just like wanda this  addresses what they're like  after the blip and keep in mind both of  them were indeed  snapped and that's something to keep in  mind because this show actually dresses  very  real things within the mcu as director  carrie skoglin said  if avengers in game was this huge  magical  out of this world story then the falcon  in the winter soldier is a very grounded  very real story it addresses things that  you really haven't thought about before  maybe in the back of your head you have  but things like where exactly do  superheroes get their money from so it's  a really good story that also  kind of has some shocks to it now it's  only the first episode so there's only  so much that can be developed but there  are a few parts during this episode  where you stop and you think  oh dang that's intense which is of  course something that you want you don't  want to be able to expect  everything you want to be surprised and  you are there are some good surprises in  this episode  some really cool that you'll really  enjoy and some that are pretty intense  like i mentioned before  and speaking of pretty intense this  episode actually does have a good amount  of  emotion in it now of course this show is  an action thriller but when it comes to  a movie or a tv  show it just can't be all action all the  time there has to be some  context behind everything there has to  be a good underlying story that gives  the action a purpose  and even though the action is amazing  and i could probably watch an entire  series just based off of action  the story and the emotion that comes  with it does back it up pretty well and  sets up what is about to happen  and i think some of the real world  actually resonates really well with what  is happening in the mcu because right  now we're in the middle of a pandemic  in the mcu they are right after the blip  right after everybody has come back  and that's something that is addressed  in this and it talks about how  it affected families and it shows the  aftermath of that again it's a very real  story  that hasn't exactly been addressed yet  we kind of got it in spider-man and far  from home but they really kind of made  light of the situation  kind of made a joke about people just  popping back up like  in the middle of a basketball game where  the band shows up which was a very  light-hearted way and kind of comedic  way to go about it because we still have  questions like  what happened to people who got dusted  in airplanes do they snap back in the  middle of the sky and fall to the ground  to their death  this episode doesn't answer that  question but it does address the effects  that the blip had  so within the falcon in the winter  soldiers first episode we have a lot of  action  that is very well done no bad cgi or  anything like that  an amazing story that goes along with it  that is a very real story about what is  actually happening within the mcu right  now  it has some surprises in it some of  which will shock you and some of which  you'll feel very very good about and be  very happy to see  it has a lot of emotion and it sets up  what is to come in the future episodes  and of course  last but not least anthony mackie and  sebastian stan of course  crushed it they've been playing these  characters for a very long time  sebastian stan has been playing bucky  since captain america the first avenger  in 2011 that's  10 years and anthony mackie has been  playing falcons since captain america  the winter soldier which was in 2014  which means he's been playing the  character for seven years so they really  know how to get into the minds of these  characters and it really does show on  screen  not just with the action and the jokes  but with the serious stuff as well  so big shout out to them and  congratulations to them for crushing  their roles  once again shout out to the director  carrie skoglin she did an amazing job  the writers all did a good job and the  cast and crew seemed to be pretty great  for the whole entire show  i loved one division i did but right now  i'd have to say that i like the falcon  and the winter soldier more and i've  only seen the first episode  i think that's primarily due to the  whole marvel field the show is much more  what we're used to so i think i like it  a little bit more due to that but  one division was still great but if  you're looking for that marvel  feel in a project you're going to love  the falcon and the winter soldier  so let me know how excited you are about  the falcon and the winter soldier in the  comments below  what do you want to see out of it be  sure to let me know and subscribe so you  don't miss out on any of the latest  videos and of course i'll be doing a  watch party tomorrow night  it'll start at 11 50 p.m pacific time  see you all there tomorrow for live  updates you can follow me on instagram  and twitter and i'm now  on tick tock doing different videos but  of course there's still marvel videos  as always thank you all so much for  watching woof  you

